## DOMAIN 1: DATA INGESTION & TRANSFORMATION (34%)

### Kinesis Decision Matrix

| Scenario | Service |
|----------|---------|
| Just deliver data A → B (S3/Redshift/OpenSearch) | Firehose (direct PUT) |
| Sub-second real-time processing | Flink (Kinesis Data Analytics) |
| Multiple independent consumers | Kinesis Data Streams + Enhanced Fan-Out |
| Stateful processing (windows, joins, aggregations) | Flink |
| Simple delivery + format conversion + partitioning | Firehose |

### Kinesis Throughput Limits (Per Shard)

| Direction | Limit |
|-----------|-------|
| Write (producer) | 1 MB/sec OR 1,000 records/sec |
| Read — WITHOUT enhanced fan-out | 2 MB/sec SHARED across ALL consumers |
| Read — WITH enhanced fan-out | 2 MB/sec PER consumer (dedicated, push-based) |
| GetRecords API calls | Max 5 per second per shard |

### Kinesis Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| ProvisionedThroughputExceededException (producer) | Increase shards (UpdateShardCount) |
| Hot shard / uneven distribution | Fix partition key (producer-side issue) |
| Consumer falling behind (high iterator age) | Scale consumer + increase retention period |
| Need multiple consumers without fan-out bottleneck | Enable Enhanced Fan-Out |

### Firehose — Complete Reference

**Supported Destinations (ONLY these 5):**
- ✅ Amazon S3
- ✅ Amazon Redshift (via S3 intermediate)
- ✅ Amazon OpenSearch Service
- ✅ Splunk
- ✅ HTTP Endpoints (custom)
- ❌ NOT: DynamoDB, RDS, Kinesis, Lambda

**Capabilities:**
- ✅ Dynamic partitioning (JQ inline OR Lambda metadata)
- ✅ Format conversion (JSON → Parquet/ORC via Glue Catalog schema)
- ✅ Lambda transformation (enrichment, DynamoDB lookups)
- ✅ Buffering (60-900 seconds interval, 1-128 MB size)
- ❌ Cannot read FROM S3 (ingestion only)
- ❌ Cannot do sub-second latency (min 60 sec buffer)

**Format Conversion Rules:**
- Schema = Glue Catalog table (strict contract)
- Extra fields in incoming data → SILENTLY DROPPED
- Missing fields in incoming data → Written as NULL
- Does NOT auto-update the catalog
- Does NOT fail on schema mismatch
- Auto-converts compatible types (string "29.99" → double)

**Error Handling:**
- Failed records → S3 backup/error bucket
- Successful records continue normally

**Firehose vs Streams → Firehose:**
- Only need delivery? → Direct PUT to Firehose (simpler, cheaper)
- Need replay/multiple consumers/real-time analytics? → Streams → Firehose

### Ingestion Service Selector

| Source Type | Service |
|-------------|---------|
| SFTP/FTP files from partners | AWS Transfer Family |
| SaaS APIs (Salesforce, Zendesk, ServiceNow) | Amazon AppFlow |
| On-premises file systems | AWS DataSync |
| Database migration (schema + data) | AWS DMS (+ SCT for heterogeneous) |
| Bulk offline transfer (multi-TB) | AWS Snowball Edge |
| Streaming data delivery | Kinesis Data Firehose |
| Database schema conversion (stored procs, views) | AWS Schema Conversion Tool (SCT) |

### AppFlow Triggers
- Schedule-based (every X minutes/hours)
- Event-based (webhooks from SaaS source)
- On-demand (manual/API)

### AWS DMS Patterns

| Scenario | Approach |
|----------|----------|
| Small dataset to Redshift (< 1 TB) | DMS direct to Redshift |
| Large dataset to Redshift (multi-TB) | DMS → S3 → COPY command |
| Ongoing replication with current state | DMS CDC → S3 → Glue with Hudi (upsert/delete) |
| Heterogeneous migration (SQL Server → Aurora) | SCT first, then DMS |

### Glue ETL — Transforms & Fixes

| Problem | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| Nested JSON → flat relational | Relationalize transform |
| Column name/position mismatch | ApplyMapping (maps by name) |
| Column data type conflicts | ResolveChoice transform |
| Slow JDBC reads | hashfield / hashexpression (parallelism) |
| Stale catalog (column not found) | Re-run Crawler |
| Reprocessing old files (batch) | Enable Job Bookmarks |
| Reprocessing records (streaming) | Configure Checkpoints (S3 location) |
| Too many small files on read | groupFiles + groupSize |
| OOM / "killed by YARN" | Switch to G.2X or G.4X workers (more memory) |
| Disk space exceeded during shuffle | Switch to G.2X workers (more disk) |
| Gradually increasing runtime (constant data) | Job Bookmarks broken — reprocessing! |
| Control output file size | maxRecordsPerFile OR repartition(n) — BOTH valid |

### Glue Streaming vs Batch

| Feature | Batch | Streaming |
|---------|-------|-----------|
| Avoid reprocessing | Job Bookmarks | Checkpoints |
| Window control | N/A | windowSize parameter |
| Exactly-once | Job Bookmarks | Checkpointing |

### Glue JDBC Parallelism

| Config | What it does |
|--------|--------------|
| hashfield | Splits reads by hashing an existing column |
| hashexpression | Splits reads using a custom expression (e.g., MOD(id, 20)) |
| Pushdown predicates | Filters rows at source (NOT for parallelism) |

### S3 Consistency (Post-December 2020)
- S3 provides **strong read-after-write consistency** for ALL operations
- EMRFS consistent view is OBSOLETE — no longer needed
- FileNotFoundException due to eventual consistency NO LONGER OCCURS

### Glue Crawler Schema Management
- Schema change policy: "Add new columns only" prevents overwriting manual fixes
- Column-level overrides protect manually corrected data types
- Next Crawler run won't overwrite your corrections

