## DOMAIN 3: DATA OPERATIONS & SUPPORT (22%)

### Step Functions Patterns

| Pattern | Use Case |
|---------|----------|
| .sync | Start task and WAIT for completion |
| .waitForTaskToken | Wait for external callback (human approval) |
| Retry | Auto-retry with MaxAttempts, IntervalSeconds, BackoffRate |
| Catch | Error handling → fallback state |
| Parallel | Run branches simultaneously, wait for ALL to complete |
| Map | Process items in a collection (loop) |
| Choice | Conditional branching (if/else) |
| TimeoutSeconds | Set generous timeout for variable-duration tasks |
| Redrive | Re-execute failed execution from point of failure |

**Trigger Step Functions from S3:**
- EventBridge rule on S3 PutObject → Step Functions (DIRECT integration, no Lambda needed)

### Airflow (MWAA)

| Task | How |
|------|-----|
| Trigger Glue job | AwsGlueJobOperator (native, auto-polls for completion) |
| Trigger EMR step | EmrAddStepsOperator + EmrStepSensor |
| Trigger Redshift query | RedshiftSQLOperator |
| Wait for S3 file | S3KeySensor |
| Re-run failed tasks | "Clear" task instances (re-runs only cleared tasks) |
| Install custom packages | requirements.txt in MWAA S3 bucket |
| Connection issues | Check security group outbound rules (port 5439 for Redshift) |

**Rule:** Always prefer native AWS operators over BashOperator/PythonOperator with CLI/boto3

### Glue Job Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| OOM / "killed by YARN" | Insufficient memory per worker | G.2X or G.4X workers |
| Disk space exceeded (shuffle) | Insufficient disk per worker | G.2X workers |
| Gradually increasing runtime | Job Bookmarks broken | Fix/enable Job Bookmarks |
| Job succeeds but empty output | Filter logic eliminating all records | Check transformation logic |
| Connection refused | Target paused or security group changed | Check network/target status |
| Streaming job not processing | Checkpoint stuck / retention expired | Reset checkpoint |

### Monitoring & Alerting

| Need | Solution |
|------|----------|
| Detect job FAILURE | EventBridge state change event (FAILED) → SNS |
| Detect slow jobs | CloudWatch metric alarm on duration |
| Detect missing data (real-time) | EventBridge S3 events → CloudWatch metric → alarm on zero |
| Data quality validation | Glue Data Quality (DQDL rules) |
| Centralized job monitoring | Glue console built-in insights (LEAST effort) |
| SLA breach warning | Track start time + alarm before deadline |

**Key Distinctions:**
- S3 Storage Lens = daily aggregate analytics (NOT real-time)
- EventBridge = real-time event detection
- "LEAST effort" = use built-in native tools first

### EventBridge Direct Targets (No Lambda Needed)
- ✅ Step Functions
- ✅ SNS
- ✅ SQS
- ✅ Lambda
- ✅ Glue Workflows
- ✅ Kinesis Data Streams
- ✅ ECS Tasks

### Pipeline Orchestration Best Practice
- Never use time-based gaps between dependent steps
- Always use orchestration (Step Functions / Airflow) with explicit dependencies
- ETL starts ONLY after Crawler/previous step completes

### Glue Workflow Triggers
- Triggers must be in "ACTIVATED" state to fire
- If Job A succeeds but Job B doesn't start → check trigger activation status

