## EXAM STRATEGY & TIPS

### Key Phrases → Answers

| If you see... | Think... |
|---------------|----------|
| "Least operational overhead" | Serverless/managed (Firehose, Athena, Serverless) |
| "Least effort" | Use built-in native features first |
| "No infrastructure management" | Athena > Redshift Serverless > EMR |
| "Zero infrastructure" + "query S3" | Athena |
| "Complex joins + fast + frequent" | Redshift (provisioned) |
| "FIPS 140-2 Level 3" | CloudHSM |
| "No internet access" | VPC Endpoints (NOT NAT Gateway) |
| "Defense-in-depth" | Combine IAM + Lake Formation |
| "Record-level deletes in data lake" | Hudi / Delta Lake |
| "SCD Type 2" | Hudi / Delta Lake |
| "Gradually increasing runtime" | Job Bookmarks broken |
| "Killed by YARN" / OOM | Increase worker memory (G.2X) |
| "Sub-second latency" | Flink (NOT Firehose) |
| "Multiple consumers" | Kinesis Data Streams + Enhanced Fan-Out |
| "Detect job failure" | EventBridge state change → SNS |
| "Schema mismatch after Crawler" | Schema change policy + column overrides |

### Common Traps to Avoid
1. ❌ Don't add Kinesis Streams in front of Firehose unless you need multiple consumers/replay
2. ❌ Don't choose Glacier for "rarely accessed" if instant retrieval is needed
3. ❌ Don't choose EVEN distribution as first fix for skew (try higher-cardinality key first)
4. ❌ Don't confuse Job Bookmarks (batch) with Checkpoints (streaming)
5. ❌ Don't assume on-demand DynamoDB = unlimited instant scaling
6. ❌ Don't choose NAT Gateway when "no internet" is required
7. ❌ Don't assume KMS key rotation re-encrypts existing data
8. ❌ Don't pick single features when the question needs multiple (LF row + column + tag)
9. ❌ Don't choose S3 Storage Lens for real-time monitoring
10. ❌ Don't forget `lakeformation:GetDataAccess` IAM permission

